const char *bc_error(bc_client_t *c);
.EE
.SH DESCRIPTION
Returns a human\-readable error message describing the last error that
occurred on the client handle \f[CR]c\f[R].
The returned string provides diagnostic detail beyond what the numeric
error codes (\f[CR]BC_ERR_*\f[R]) convey.
.PP
The returned pointer refers to an internal static buffer within the
client handle.
The caller must NOT free it.
The contents of the buffer are overwritten on the next API call that
modifies error state on the same handle.
.PP
If no error has occurred, the function returns an empty string
(\f[CR]\(dq\(dq\f[R]), not NULL.
